# Next.js App Router Patterns

- Default to Server Components in `app/`; add `"use client"` only when hooks, browser APIs, or event handlers are required.
- Keep route segments thin: move reusable UI to `components/*` and data logic to dedicated modules.
- Keep components small and feature-focused; extract subcomponents/hooks/services instead of growing generic "do everything" components.
- Use `notFound()` and `redirect()` for control flow instead of manual fallback rendering.
- Keep metadata colocated with route segments via `metadata` or `generateMetadata`.
- Prefer server-side data loading for initial page render; hydrate client state only when interactivity is needed.
- Use route groups and nested layouts to keep shared chrome out of page-level components.
- Validate search params and dynamic params before usage to avoid implicit runtime assumptions.
- Keep loading and error states explicit with `loading.tsx` and `error.tsx` where appropriate.
